Circuit Architecture
The complete timing circuit consists of three primary modules:

Clock & Reset Circuitry: Generates a continuous 
100
 MHz
100 MHz square wave (
5
 ns
5 ns high, 
5
 ns
5 ns low) and a single 
10
 ns
10 ns active-high pulse on power-up.
Program Counter (PC) Register with Adder: Synchronous register with asynchronous/synchronous reset to 0 and a constant adder (
+
4
+4) on the feedback path.
Execution Pipeline Control: Enables Instruction Memory read and ALU execution based on clock phase aligned with the PC updates.
Here is a diagram showing the digital logic and component interconnects for this timing circuit:graph TD
    CLK_GEN[100 MHz Osc<br/>T = 10ns] -->|CLK| PC[Program Counter Reg]
    CLK_GEN -->|CLK| ALU[ALU Control]
    
    POR[POR / Monostable<br/>0-10ns Reset Pulse] -->|Reset| PC
    
    PC -->|PC Output| ADD[Adder +4]
    ADD -->|PC + 4| MUX[Reset Mux]
    POR -->|Select| MUX
    MUX -->|Next PC| PC
    
    PC -->|Address| IMEM[Instruction Memory]
    IMEM -->|Instruction| ALU
    ALU -->|Result| OUT[ALU Output Valid @ 30-40ns]
